{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B97udgkbvcfdHcgACiWv1W","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR; long paper 8-page limit + unlimited refs)\n5\t- Page limit: 8 pages main text (当前 10 页，需压缩 2 页)\n6\t\n7\t## Paper Type\n8\tEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n9\t\n10\t## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n11\t\n12\t**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n13\t- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%), plan_027 (temporal ability overlap: d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%; 1:1 NN matching C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp; contrast with Llama-2v3 d=-0.99→matched C%=28.3%, where ability confound explains 33pp)\n14\t- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n15\t- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n16\t\n17\t**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. **Empirically validated** (plan_026): direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on 9,229 MMLU items shows enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, Phi=0.012, χ²=1.28 (p=0.258), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15]. Consistent across subtypes (input_only: 0.986, input_and_label: 0.960). Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n18\t- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_026 (direct comparison: enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, p=0.258), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n19\t- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\" — now with direct empirical evidence, not just conceptual argument\n20\t\n21\t**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n22\t- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n23\t- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n24\t- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n25\t\n26\t**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n27\t1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n28\t2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n29\t3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n30\t4. **Cross-benchmark validation (exploratory)**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33). **DEMOTED to exploratory** per Dream #6 three-tier consensus: N=33, CI wide [−0.71, −0.16], not strong enough for numbered contribution. This evidence is suggestive but should NOT appear in abstract/conclusion as core support.\n31\t- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n32\t- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227). plan_020 circularity ablation is the second pillar. GSM1K correlation (plan_004 Step 3) is supplementary/exploratory only.\n33\t- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n34\t- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n35\t\n36\t## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n37\t\n38\t**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n39\t\n40\t**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n41\t\n42\t**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n43\t\n44\t1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n45\t\n46\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n47\t\n48\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n49\t\n50\t4. **DIF as diagnostic lens + actionable protocol**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. **Actionable contribution**: DIF audit protocol for benchmark maintainers (monitoring frequency, decision rules, response options).\n51\t\n52\t**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF serves as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations, with a concrete audit protocol for benchmark maintenance.\"\n53\t\n54\t## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n55\t\n56\t**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n57\t- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n58\t- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n59\t- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n60\t- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n61\t- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n62\t- §6 Conclusion\n63\t\n64\t**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n65\t- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n66\t- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n67\t- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n68\t- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n69\t- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n70\t- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n71\t- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n72\t- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n73\t\n74\t## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n75\t\n76\tSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n77\t\n78\t## Venue Fit\n79\t\n80\t- **EMNLP 2026**: Strong fit — NLP evaluation methodology is a dedicated area, reviewers expect empirical studies of benchmarks. \"Empirical, not algorithmic\" contribution type well-received. Risk: 8-page limit requires significant compression (current 10 pages). Mitigation: move structural analysis details to appendix.\n81\t\n82\t## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n83\t\n84\tMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n85\t\n86\t1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n87\t\n88\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n89\t\n90\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n91\t\n92\t**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n93\t\n94\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n95\t\n96\t1. **\"31% could just mean models got better / ability confound inflates C%\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019 + plan_027). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). Temporal cohort ability gap is negligible (d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%); 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01) yields C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp. Contrast: Llama-2v3 (d=-0.99) drops from 61.3% to 28.3% under matching. Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF.\n97\t\n98\t2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n99\t\n100\t3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n101\t\n102\t4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n103\t\n104\t5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). **plan_028 in progress**: checking METABENCH for ARC/HellaSwag/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA response matrices to run multi-benchmark temporal DIF. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work if METABENCH lacks other benchmarks.\n105\t\n106\t6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n107\t\n108\t7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n109\t\n110\t8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n111\t\n112\t9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n113\t\n114\t10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n115\t\n116\t11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n117\t\n118\t## Dropped from Original Framing\n119\t\n120\t- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n121\t- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n122\t- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n123\t- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68384416-f199-481e-b490-5f37e9ab5fc0","uuid":"415a661a-5b8c-4d6d-b8b5-81d25a86b62f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:46:01.960Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T141728/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR; long paper 8-page limit + unlimited refs)\n- Page limit: 8 pages main text (当前 10 页，需压缩 2 页)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n\n## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%), plan_027 (temporal ability overlap: d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%; 1:1 NN matching C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp; contrast with Llama-2v3 d=-0.99→matched C%=28.3%, where ability confound explains 33pp)\n- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n\n**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. **Empirically validated** (plan_026): direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on 9,229 MMLU items shows enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, Phi=0.012, χ²=1.28 (p=0.258), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15]. Consistent across subtypes (input_only: 0.986, input_and_label: 0.960). Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_026 (direct comparison: enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, p=0.258), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\" — now with direct empirical evidence, not just conceptual argument\n\n**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n\n**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n4. **Cross-benchmark validation (exploratory)**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33). **DEMOTED to exploratory** per Dream #6 three-tier consensus: N=33, CI wide [−0.71, −0.16], not strong enough for numbered contribution. This evidence is suggestive but should NOT appear in abstract/conclusion as core support.\n- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227). plan_020 circularity ablation is the second pillar. GSM1K correlation (plan_004 Step 3) is supplementary/exploratory only.\n- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n\n## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n\n**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n\n**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n\n**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n\n1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n\n4. **DIF as diagnostic lens + actionable protocol**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. **Actionable contribution**: DIF audit protocol for benchmark maintainers (monitoring frequency, decision rules, response options).\n\n**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF serves as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations, with a concrete audit protocol for benchmark maintenance.\"\n\n## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n\n**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n- §6 Conclusion\n\n**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n\n## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n\nSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\n- **EMNLP 2026**: Strong fit — NLP evaluation methodology is a dedicated area, reviewers expect empirical studies of benchmarks. \"Empirical, not algorithmic\" contribution type well-received. Risk: 8-page limit requires significant compression (current 10 pages). Mitigation: move structural analysis details to appendix.\n\n## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n\nMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n\n1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n\n**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n\n1. **\"31% could just mean models got better / ability confound inflates C%\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019 + plan_027). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). Temporal cohort ability gap is negligible (d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%); 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01) yields C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp. Contrast: Llama-2v3 (d=-0.99) drops from 61.3% to 28.3% under matching. Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF.\n\n2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n\n3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n\n4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n\n5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). **plan_028 in progress**: checking METABENCH for ARC/HellaSwag/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA response matrices to run multi-benchmark temporal DIF. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work if METABENCH lacks other benchmarks.\n\n6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n\n7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n\n8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n\n9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n\n10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n\n11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n\n## Dropped from Original Framing\n\n- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TXRRwinQe8PNu2yMCfvHsL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"对METABENCH MMLU响应矩阵（5219模型×12508题目）进行MH-DIF分析。包括temporal cohort split (2023 vs 2024-H1)、ability-quintile split、within-family confound control (Llama-2 vs Llama-3)、domain-specificity分析、Li et al. web-overlap proxy验证。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"temporal_cohort\": {\n7\t        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n8\t        \"n_foc\": 807,\n9\t        \"ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n10\t        \"ets_b_pct\": 20.5,\n11\t        \"ets_a_pct\": 48.2,\n12\t        \"mean_delta_mh_c_items\": 2.14,\n13\t        \"median_delta_mh_c_items\": 1.78\n14\t      },\n15\t      \"ability_cohort\": {\n16\t        \"ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n17\t        \"enrichment\": 1.19\n18\t      },\n19\t      \"within_family\": {\n20\t        \"llama2_vs_llama3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n21\t        \"mistral_vs_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n22\t        \"llama_jaccard_with_temporal\": 0.28\n23\t      },\n24\t      \"domain_specificity\": {\n25\t        \"spearman_rho_acc_improvement_vs_c_pct\": 0.307,\n26\t        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n27\t        \"n_subjects\": 57,\n28\t        \"all_subjects_have_dif\": true,\n29\t        \"c_pct_range\": [\n30\t          20.7,\n31\t          48.4\n32\t        ]\n33\t      },\n34\t      \"proxy_validation\": {\n35\t        \"li_et_al_coverage\": 0.738,\n36\t        \"enrichment_temporal\": 0.96,\n37\t        \"fpr_li_clean_temporal\": 0.318,\n38\t        \"enrichment_ability\": 1.19,\n39\t        \"fpr_li_clean_ability\": 0.027\n40\t      },\n41\t      \"sanity_check\": {\n42\t        \"random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n43\t        \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n44\t      }\n45\t    },\n46\t    \"tables\": [\n47\t      {\n48\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary\",\n49\t        \"content\": \"4-way sensitivity matrix: cohort × item filtering → C% values\"\n50\t      },\n51\t      {\n52\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Domain-Specificity\",\n53\t        \"content\": \"57 subjects × C% × accuracy improvement correlation\"\n54\t      }\n55\t    ],\n56\t    \"figures\": [],\n57\t    \"analysis\": \"核心结果solid。Median档reviewers的主要friction点：(1) within-family Llama-2v3的C%=61.3% 远高于temporal 31.3%，需要解释为什么family comparison不是更好的design；(2) domain ρ=0.307 虽然p=0.02但effect size modest，需要plan_019 item-level decomposition作为补充； (3) Li et al. proxy validation的\\\"negative result\\\"需要更清晰的framing——是validation failure 还是expected orthogonality。8页压缩下within-family detail可能被移入appendix。\\n\\n\\n在median档位下，31.3% C%是核心发现，被Claim 1直接支撑。Reviewers接受这个数字的statistical significance（random split仅0.18%），但至少1位reviewer要求更强的causal language hedging—— 因为within-family分析（Llama-2 vs Llama-3 C%=61.3%）显示family-level capability jump也会 产生高DIF，temporal cohort的31.3%可能混合了genuine item instability和capability-driven DIF。 ρ=0.307的domain-level correlation被接受为modest ecological correlation，但reviewer要求 明确\\\"item-level decomposition shows only 2.4pp explained\\\"（来自plan_019/030）。 Enrichment≈0.96支撑Claim 2但被1位reviewer视为\\\"expected by construction\\\"。Ability cohort 的2.9% C%作为negative control被接受。\\n\"\n58\t  },\n59\t  {\n60\t    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n61\t    \"description\": \"验证DIF对reasoning-RL模型的鲁棒性。从METABENCH筛选alignment-RL模型（DPO/ORPO，N≈477）， 外加10-15个open-weight reasoning-RL模型（GRPO/PPO），测试DIF检测稳定性并与传统检测器对比。\\n\",\n62\t    \"results\": {\n63\t      \"alignment_rl_cohort\": {\n64\t        \"n_models\": 477,\n65\t        \"c_pct_with_alignment_rl\": 31.1,\n66\t        \"c_pct_without\": 31.3,\n67\t        \"jaccard_flags_overlap\": 0.968,\n68\t        \"flag_stability\": \"negligible change\"\n69\t      },\n70\t      \"reasoning_rl_models\": {\n71\t        \"n_available\": 13,\n72\t        \"models_tested\": [\n73\t          \"deepseek-r1-7b\",\n74\t          \"deepseek-r1-32b\",\n75\t          \"qwen2.5-rl-7b\",\n76\t          \"qwen2.5-rl-14b\",\n77\t          \"qwen2.5-rl-32b\",\n78\t          \"o1-mini-proxy\",\n79\t          \"skywork-or1-8b\",\n80\t          \"open-reasoner-7b\",\n81\t          \"marco-o1-7b\",\n82\t          \"k2-65b\",\n83\t          \"rstar-math-7b\",\n84\t          \"still-2-1.5b\",\n85\t          \"llemma-rl-7b\"\n86\t        ],\n87\t        \"c_pct_with_rl_in_focal\": 31.0,\n88\t        \"c_pct_change\": -0.3,\n89\t        \"jaccard_with_vs_without_rl\": 0.971\n90\t      },\n91\t      \"traditional_detector_comparison\": {\n92\t        \"mink_auroc_non_rl\": 0.714,\n93\t        \"mink_auroc_rl_models\": 0.528,\n94\t        \"mink_auroc_delta\": -0.186,\n95\t        \"constat_auroc_non_rl\": 0.681,\n96\t        \"constat_auroc_rl_models\": 0.513,\n97\t        \"constat_auroc_delta\": -0.168,\n98\t        \"dif_retention_ratio\": 0.987\n99\t      },\n100\t      \"statistical_tests\": {\n101\t        \"delong_mink_p\": 0.089,\n102\t        \"delong_constat_p\": 0.112,\n103\t        \"tost_equivalence\": \"inconclusive (CI: [-0.04, 0.07], bounds ±0.10)\",\n104\t        \"bootstrap_ci_dif_retention\": [\n105\t          0.93,\n106\t          1.03\n107\t        ]\n108\t      },\n109\t      \"power_analysis\": {\n110\t        \"partial_exploitation_p04\": \"delta_MH≈0.84, TPR≈0.31\",\n111\t        \"partial_exploitation_p07\": \"delta_MH≈1.18, TPR≈0.52\",\n112\t        \"partial_exploitation_p10\": \"delta_MH≈1.68, TPR≈0.76\",\n113\t        \"detection_boundary\": \"p≈0.55 for TPR≥0.50 at N=100\"\n114\t      }\n115\t    },\n116\t    \"tables\": [\n117\t      {\n118\t        \"name\": \"Table S1 (Appendix): RL Robustness Comparison\",\n119\t        \"content\": \"AUROC comparison across DIF/Min-K%/ConStat × model type (non-RL, alignment-RL, reasoning-RL)\"\n120\t      }\n121\t    ],\n122\t    \"figures\": [],\n123\t    \"analysis\": \"N=13是致命弱点。实验方向正确但statistical power不足以支撑numbered claim。 Median档策略：在limitations中honest disclosure \\\"reasoning-RL robustness remains an open question due to limited open-weight availability\\\"，同时在main text保留 alignment-RL的positive result（N=477，C% stable at 31.1%）作为partial evidence。 Reviewer不会因此reject但会在score中扣分（contributes to 3.25-3.75 range）。\\n\\n\\nMedian档位的关键限制：reasoning-RL模型仅13个，远低于统计显著性所需的样本量。DIF是group-level 方法，将13个RL模型混入N≈807的focal cohort几乎不改变C%（31.3%→31.0%），但这也意味着无法 单独评估RL模型的DIF特性。传统检测器（Min-K%，ConStat）在RL模型上的AUROC下降（0.71→0.53, 0.68→0.51），方向支持\\\"DIF比per-model方法更robust\\\"的claim，但DeLong test p>0.05因为N=13 power不足。TOST等价性检验inconclusive——CI包含零但也包含meaningful differences。 在median档下，这个实验被降级到Limitations section作为\\\"directional evidence\\\"， reviewers接受reasoning-RL是emerging phenomenon、数据有限的framing，但1位reviewer 标注\\\"this weakens the practical relevance claim for post-2024 models\\\"。\\n\"\n124\t  },\n125\t  {\n126\t    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n127\t    \"description\": \"独立评估ConStat-style perturbation testing在MMLU上的检测力。需要GPU生成语义等价 reformulations并收集模型响应。\\n\",\n128\t    \"results\": {\n129\t      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n130\t      \"reason\": \"GPU budget constraint (80h required) + 依赖LLM paraphrasing pipeline未搭建\",\n131\t      \"counterfactual_if_executed\": {\n132\t        \"n_items_reformulated\": 250,\n133\t        \"constat_fdr_controlled_detection_rate\": 0.42,\n134\t        \"constat_auroc_non_rl\": 0.68,\n135\t        \"constat_auroc_rl\": 0.51,\n136\t        \"constat_dif_overlap_jaccard\": 0.18,\n137\t        \"constat_specificity\": \"high for verbatim contamination, low for capability-driven DIF\"\n138\t      }\n139\t    },\n140\t    \"tables\": [],\n141\t    \"figures\": [],\n142\t    \"analysis\": \"未执行。对median档outcome的影响：1位reviewer在minor comments中提到\\\"direct comparison with ConStat would strengthen the paper\\\"，但接受conceptual distinction argument。 不是core weakness。\\n\\n\\n在median档位下，plan_003a未执行是合理的——paper已pivot away from ensemble detection (Claim 2 old) toward diagnostic framing。GPU预算优先分配给plan_002和plan_004。 ConStat/DVD的AUROC数字已通过文献引用在main text中提供（Blebea et al. 2024）， 无需独立复现。Reviewers可能要求\\\"why not compare directly\\\"但rebuttal可以指向 ConStat的public results + 不同detection targets（perturbation sensitivity vs differential functioning）的conceptual argument。在median档下这不构成reject reason 但contributes to \\\"thin empirical comparison\\\" concern。\\n\"\n143\t  },\n144\t  {\n145\t    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n146\t    \"description\": \"独立评估DVD generation variance在MMLU上的检测力。需要GPU对10-15个模型生成50次响应。\\n\",\n147\t    \"results\": {\n148\t      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n149\t      \"reason\": \"GPU budget constraint (70h required) + 需要open-weight model inference pipeline\",\n150\t      \"counterfactual_if_executed\": {\n151\t        \"n_models\": 12,\n152\t        \"responses_per_item\": 50,\n153\t        \"dvd_detection_rate\": 0.35,\n154\t        \"dvd_auroc\": 0.62,\n155\t        \"dvd_variant_contamination_sensitivity\": 0.71,\n156\t        \"dvd_verbatim_contamination_sensitivity\": 0.44\n157\t      }\n158\t    },\n159\t    \"tables\": [],\n160\t    \"figures\": [],\n161\t    \"analysis\": \"未执行。影响与plan_003a类似，合并为一个reviewer concern：\\\"existing method comparison is conceptual rather than empirical\\\"。Median档下这是minor issue，不影响accept/reject。\\n\\n\\n与plan_003a相同逻辑——paper不再追求ensemble detection，DVD作为independent baseline 的value在current framing下降低。Median档reviewers理解GPU constraint但可能在 \\\"comparison with existing methods\\\" section标注insufficiency。Rebuttal中可指向 DVD原始论文结果 + \\\"DIF operates at group level while DVD operates at model level, complementary rather than competing\\\"。\\n\"\n162\t  },\n163\t  {\n164\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n165\t    \"description\": \"融合DIF + ConStat + DVD为多信号ensemble。依赖plan_003a和plan_003b。\\n\",\n166\t    \"results\": {\n167\t      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n168\t      \"reason\": \"Dependencies plan_003a and plan_003b not executed; ensemble claim dropped from paper\",\n169\t      \"paper_status\": \"Dropped to future work section\"\n170\t    },\n171\t    \"tables\": [],\n172\t    \"figures\": [],\n173\t    \"analysis\": \"完全dropped。无直接影响，但间接加剧Claim 4 actionability的weakness——如果ensemble 存在，actionability story会更强。Median档下这是background weakness，不是explicit reviewer complaint。\\n\\n\\nPlan_003c在paper pivot后被完全dropped。Paper从\\\"we detect contamination better via ensemble\\\"转向\\\"we characterize benchmark properties via DIF\\\"。Median档reviewers 不会miss这个experiment因为paper不再claim ensemble contribution。但1位reviewer 可能在\\\"future work\\\"评论中写\\\"the ensemble direction seems promising and its absence weakens the practical impact\\\"——这contributes to actionability concern。\\n\"\n174\t  },\n175\t  {\n176\t    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n177\t    \"description\": \"在GSM8K上复现DIF分析，使用GSM1K作为contamination ground truth。包括temporal DIF、 semi-synthetic validation、GSM1K correlation三步。\\n\",\n178\t    \"results\": {\n179\t      \"step1_temporal_dif\": {\n180\t        \"n_items\": 1319,\n181\t        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n182\t        \"n_foc\": 804,\n183\t        \"standard_c_pct\": 18.9,\n184\t        \"external_c_pct\": 47.4,\n185\t        \"sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n186\t        \"standard_external_spearman\": 0.926\n187\t      },\n188\t      \"step2_semi_synthetic\": {\n189\t        \"standard_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n190\t        \"standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n191\t        \"external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n192\t        \"fpr_stable\": true\n193\t      },\n194\t      \"step3_gsm1k_correlation\": {\n195\t        \"n_matched_models\": 33,\n196\t        \"pearson_r\": -0.478,\n197\t        \"pearson_p\": 0.005,\n198\t        \"spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n199\t        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n200\t        \"partial_r_controlling_accuracy\": -0.385,\n201\t        \"partial_p\": 0.027,\n202\t        \"direction\": \"NEGATIVE — opposite to naive contamination hypothesis\",\n203\t        \"interpretation\": \"DIF-C items ANTI-correlate with contamination gap; DIF captures capability differential, not contamination per se\",\n204\t        \"ci_95_pearson\": [\n205\t          -0.71,\n206\t          -0.16\n207\t        ],\n208\t        \"ci_95_spearman\": [\n209\t          -0.66,\n210\t          -0.03\n211\t        ],\n212\t        \"cook_d_max\": \"deepseek-math-7b-rl\",\n213\t        \"leave_one_out_robust\": true\n214\t      }\n215\t    },\n216\t    \"tables\": [\n217\t      {\n218\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Cross-Benchmark DIF Summary\",\n219\t        \"content\": \"GSM8K temporal DIF: C%=18.9%, ΔTPR=+0.818, GSM1K r=-0.478\"\n220\t      }\n221\t    ],\n222\t    \"figures\": [],\n223\t    \"analysis\": \"Mixed result。Semi-synthetic validation强化Claim 3，但GSM1K negative correlation + lower C%创造了tension。Median档reviewers接受\\\"DIF captures differential functioning broadly, not just contamination\\\"的framing，但GSM1K result被从abstract/conclusion 移除。HellaSwag C%=17.9%（来自plan_028）进一步支持\\\"lower rates on non-MMLU benchmarks\\\" 的pattern，给reviewer ammunition质疑MMLU-specificity。\\n\\n\\nGSM8K的C%=18.9%显著低于MMLU的31.3%，在median档下被1位reviewer质疑为\\\"DIF may be benchmark-specific — lower rates on math benchmarks suggest the phenomenon is modulated by domain characteristics\\\"。这是valid concern因为GSM8K是单领域数学题， item homogeneity高于MMLU的57-subject结构。GSM1K correlation的r=-0.478方向为负 （与contamination hypothesis相反），被demoted to exploratory per Dream #6 consensus。 N=33 + wide CI [-0.71, -0.16]使这个结果在median档下不被视为strong evidence。 Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=+0.818则是positive result，支撑Claim 3的framework portability。 Median档下Step 2被接受，Step 3被标注\\\"exploratory, underpowered\\\"。\\n\"\n224\t  },\n225\t  {\n226\t    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n227\t    \"description\": \"在MMLU上拟合bifactor IRT模型（general factor + 57 subject-specific factors），选择 anchor items进行fixed-parameter calibration equating。\\n\",\n228\t    \"results\": {\n229\t      \"status\": \"attempted_and_killed\",\n230\t      \"convergence\": {\n231\t        \"full_57_subject\": \"failed to converge after 5000 EM iterations\",\n232\t        \"reduced_10_subject\": \"converged but poor fit\",\n233\t        \"reduced_5_subject\": \"converged, marginal fit\"\n234\t      },\n235\t      \"fit_statistics_5_subject\": {\n236\t        \"rmsea\": 0.078,\n237\t        \"cfi\": 0.724,\n238\t        \"tli\": 0.698,\n239\t        \"srmr\": 0.091\n240\t      },\n241\t      \"anchor_item_selection\": {\n242\t        \"n_candidate_anchors\": 312,\n243\t        \"anchor_stability_criterion\": \"DIF A-class + discrimination > 0.8\",\n244\t        \"anchor_coverage\": \"38/57 subjects represented\"\n245\t      },\n246\t      \"equating_pilot\": {\n247\t        \"status\": \"abandoned — fit insufficient for reliable equating\",\n248\t        \"rho_equated_vs_original\": null,\n249\t        \"decision\": \"killed; within-subject DIF (plan_014) provides alternative without requiring full IRT model\"\n250\t      }\n251\t    },\n252\t    \"tables\": [],\n253\t    \"figures\": [],\n254\t    \"analysis\": \"Expected failure。在median档下被移入limitations section作为\\\"our attempts to improve IRT model specification did not succeed, but within-subject validation (plan_014) confirms DIF findings are not artifacts of cross-subject matching\\\"。Contributes to the \\\"three structural constraints\\\" narrative。不直接影响reviewer score。\\n\\n\\nBifactor IRT在MMLU上失败是structurally predictable的：57个subjects × 12508 items的 bifactor model需要估计~57 specific factors + 1 general factor + ~25000 item parameters， 计算上不可行且psychometrically questionable（MMLU的57 subjects不是designed dimensions）。 在median档下，这个failure被report为\\\"empirical observation that motivates future multidimensional IRT work\\\"，positioned as honest negative result。Plan_014的 within-subject DIF（C%=38.1%）提供了alternative path证明DIF不依赖于cross-subject matching artifact。Reviewer可能质疑\\\"why attempt bifactor at all\\\"但不会因failure 扣分——negative results是legitimate contribution if honestly reported。\\n\"\n255\t  },\n256\t  {\n257\t    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n258\t    \"description\": \"为DIF-flagged MMLU items生成替换题目，通过student simulation进行difficulty calibration。\\n\",\n259\t    \"results\": {\n260\t      \"status\": \"blocked\",\n261\t      \"blocking_dependency\": \"plan_005 (bifactor IRT) killed — no equating framework for calibration\",\n262\t      \"alternative_path\": \"plan_032 DIF-cleaned demonstration provides actionability evidence without item replacement\",\n263\t      \"counterfactual_if_executed\": {\n264\t        \"n_items_generated\": 500,\n265\t        \"difficulty_correlation_prompt\": 0.32,\n266\t        \"difficulty_correlation_simulation\": 0.71,\n267\t        \"construct_fidelity_human_eval\": 0.64,\n268\t        \"replacement_set_rho_vs_original\": 0.989\n269\t      }\n270\t    },\n271\t    \"tables\": [],\n272\t    \"figures\": [],\n273\t    \"analysis\": \"Blocked。Paper已完全pivot away from regeneration claim。在median档下无影响。\\n\\n\\nPlan_006被plan_005 failure阻塞是合理的——没有可靠的IRT equating framework， replacement items无法calibrated到同一量表上。在median档下，paper不claim \\\"benchmark regeneration\\\"（已从original framing dropped），改为claim \\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"。Plan_032的DIF-cleaned demonstration（89.5% models shift ≥5 ranks, z=8.5 vs random）提供了不需要item replacement的actionability evidence。Reviewers不会miss这个experiment因为paper不再promise regeneration。\\n\"\n274\t  },\n275\t  {\n276\t    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n277\t    \"description\": \"实现Sinharay et al. (2006)的cumulative Bayesian DIF priors，模拟4次连续benchmark administrations，展示累积evidence带来的power improvement。\\n\",\n278\t    \"results\": {\n279\t      \"simulation_design\": {\n280\t        \"n_administrations\": 4,\n281\t        \"n_items_per_admin\": 500,\n282\t        \"n_models_per_admin\": 200,\n283\t        \"effect_sizes\": [\n284\t          0.8,\n285\t          1.0,\n286\t          1.2,\n287\t          1.4,\n288\t          1.6\n289\t        ],\n290\t        \"contamination_prevalence\": 0.15\n291\t      },\n292\t      \"power_results\": {\n293\t        \"single_admin_tpr_d10\": 0.397,\n294\t        \"cumulative_2_admin_tpr_d10\": 0.548,\n295\t        \"cumulative_3_admin_tpr_d10\": 0.681,\n296\t        \"cumulative_4_admin_tpr_d10\": 0.739,\n297\t        \"single_admin_tpr_d14\": 0.682,\n298\t        \"cumulative_3_admin_tpr_d14\": 0.841\n299\t      },\n300\t      \"fpr_all_conditions\": \"<0.06\",\n301\t      \"prior_weight_sensitivity\": {\n302\t        \"informative_prior_tpr_3admin\": 0.681,\n303\t        \"flat_prior_tpr_3admin\": 0.523,\n304\t        \"prior_impact\": \"+0.158 TPR from informative priors\"\n305\t      },\n306\t      \"bayes_factor_threshold\": {\n307\t        \"bf_gt_3_pct_3admin\": 0.58,\n308\t        \"bf_gt_10_pct_3admin\": 0.41\n309\t      }\n310\t    },\n311\t    \"tables\": [\n312\t      {\n313\t        \"name\": \"Table S2 (Appendix): Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power\",\n314\t        \"content\": \"TPR × n_administrations × effect_size matrix + BF threshold analysis\"\n315\t      }\n316\t    ],\n317\t    \"figures\": [],\n318\t    \"analysis\": \"Simulation-only结果在median档下被视为supplementary。主要value是为Discussion中 \\\"longitudinal benchmark monitoring protocol\\\"提供quantitative grounding。 不直接影响reviewer score但strengthens the \\\"audit protocol\\\" narrative for Claim 4。\\n\\n\\nCumulative Bayesian DIF在simulation中表现符合预期：3次administration后power从0.40 提升到0.68（δ=1.0），符合Sinharay et al.的理论预测。但这是pure simulation——没有在 real METABENCH data上进行temporal sliding window validation。在median档下， 这个experiment被放入appendix作为\\\"methodological extension for longitudinal benchmark monitoring\\\"。Reviewers将其视为incremental：1位reviewer写\\\"the Bayesian accumulation is a known technique; the contribution here is applying it to the LLM context, which is straightforward\\\"。Proposition 1的formal proof（cross-subject ΔFPR=0） 被同一位reviewer称为\\\"incremental\\\"——这两个方法贡献合并被视为不够novel。\\n\"\n319\t  },\n320\t  {\n321\t    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n322\t    \"description\": \"分析benchmark在progressive item replacement下的validity degradation。模拟5%-50% replacement rate，测量ranking stability、score reliability、construct coverage。\\n\",\n323\t    \"results\": {\n324\t      \"replacement_rates\": [\n325\t        0.05,\n326\t        0.1,\n327\t        0.15,\n328\t        0.2,\n329\t        0.3,\n330\t        0.5\n331\t      ],\n332\t      \"ranking_stability_rho\": {\n333\t        \"pct_05\": 0.9994,\n334\t        \"pct_10\": 0.9981,\n335\t        \"pct_15\": 0.9963,\n336\t        \"pct_20\": 0.9938,\n337\t        \"pct_30\": 0.9867,\n338\t        \"pct_50\": 0.9714\n339\t      },\n340\t      \"score_reliability_alpha\": {\n341\t        \"original\": 0.962,\n342\t        \"pct_05\": 0.959,\n343\t        \"pct_10\": 0.955,\n344\t        \"pct_15\": 0.95,\n345\t        \"pct_20\": 0.944,\n346\t        \"pct_30\": 0.929,\n347\t        \"pct_50\": 0.898\n348\t      },\n349\t      \"construct_coverage\": {\n350\t        \"pct_subjects_ge80pct_items_at_20pct\": 0.947,\n351\t        \"pct_subjects_ge80pct_items_at_50pct\": 0.614,\n352\t        \"first_subject_below_80pct\": \"formal_logic (N=126, loses >25 items at 20%)\"\n353\t      },\n354\t      \"theoretical_bound\": {\n355\t        \"rho_lower_bound_at_r\": \"ρ ≥ 1 - r × (1 - α_replacement) / α_original, approximate\",\n356\t        \"validity_threshold\": \"ρ < 0.99 at ~22% replacement for MMLU\"\n357\t      },\n358\t      \"comparison_with_plan_032\": {\n359\t        \"plan_032_rho\": 0.9965,\n360\t        \"graceful_degradation_predicted_rho_at_31pct\": 0.9856,\n361\t        \"discrepancy\": \"DIF-targeted removal is LESS disruptive than random replacement (0.9965 > 0.9856), consistent with plan_020 circularity ablation\"\n362\t      }\n363\t    },\n364\t    \"tables\": [\n365\t      {\n366\t        \"name\": \"Table S3 (Appendix): Graceful Degradation Metrics\",\n367\t        \"content\": \"Replacement rate × ρ × α × construct coverage matrix\"\n368\t      }\n369\t    ],\n370\t    \"figures\": [],\n371\t    \"analysis\": \"Clean supplementary result。在median档下strengthens \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative但simultaneously feeds reviewer skepticism about practical significance。 这是median档的核心tension：数据越是显示ranking robustness，actionability argument 越难卖。\\n\\n\\nGraceful degradation分析在median档下支撑\\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\"叙事：即使移除31% items，ρ仍>0.98（random replacement）或>0.996（DIF-targeted removal）。这与plan_017 的ρ=0.997一致。但reviewer的tension点恰恰在这里：\\\"if benchmark is this redundant, what's the practical value of identifying unstable items?\\\"至少1位reviewer质疑 actionability——31% items unstable but rankings barely change，所以who cares？ Plan_032的cohort asymmetry（2024 Δrank=+73.6）是回应这个质疑的ammunition，但 在median档下论证力度不够——reviewer要求control for model quality confound。 Graceful degradation本身被接受为clean supplementary analysis但被移入appendix。\\n\"\n372\t  },\n373\t  {\n374\t    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n375\t    \"description\": \"实现Tutz & Berger (2016) Item-Focused Trees作为categorical DIF的alternative， 将model release date作为continuous covariate。\\n\",\n376\t    \"results\": {\n377\t      \"model\": {\n378\t        \"splitting_variable\": \"release_date (continuous, days since 2023-01-01)\",\n379\t        \"tree_depth\": 3,\n380\t        \"n_terminal_nodes\": 5,\n381\t        \"primary_split\": \"2023-08-15 (separating early-2023 from late-2023+)\",\n382\t        \"secondary_split\": \"2024-02-01 (within late-2023+ group)\"\n383\t      },\n384\t      \"dif_detection\": {\n385\t        \"n_items_significant\": 3421,\n386\t        \"pct_items_significant\": 27.4,\n387\t        \"overlap_with_mh_c\": 0.823,\n388\t        \"jaccard_with_mh_c\": 0.691,\n389\t        \"items_only_ift\": 487,\n390\t        \"items_only_mh\": 984\n391\t      },\n392\t      \"temporal_gradient\": {\n393\t        \"effect_size_vs_time_distance_r\": 0.312,\n394\t        \"effect_size_vs_time_distance_p\": \"<0.001\",\n395\t        \"early_2023_vs_late_2024_mean_dif\": 1.87,\n396\t        \"adjacent_half_years_mean_dif\": 0.94\n397\t      },\n398\t      \"model_fit\": {\n399\t        \"deviance_explained_r2\": 0.031,\n400\t        \"aic_vs_categorical\": \"IFT AIC=48921 vs MH-categorical AIC=49103 (marginal improvement)\"\n401\t      },\n402\t      \"conclusion\": \"IFT confirms temporal gradient but adds limited explanatory power beyond categorical MH\"\n403\t    },\n404\t    \"tables\": [\n405\t      {\n406\t        \"name\": \"Table S4 (Appendix): IFT vs MH-DIF Comparison\",\n407\t        \"content\": \"Item overlap, detection rates, split points\"\n408\t      }\n409\t    ],\n410\t    \"figures\": [],\n411\t    \"analysis\": \"Supplementary robustness check。Median档下reviewers不explicitly request这个分析 但它preemptively addresses \\\"arbitrary cohort boundary\\\" concern。Value在于showing temporal DIF是gradient而非artifact of specific cutoff。被appendix化对page budget 有利。\\n\\n\\nIFT在median档下是\\\"nice to have\\\"的robustness check。与MH-DIF的82.3% overlap确认 categorical temporal split不是arbitrary——continuous analysis recovers similar items。 Primary split at ~2023-08-15大致对应LLM rapid improvement期（Llama-2 release附近）， 但R²=0.031说明release date alone解释DIF variation极少。Reviewer视为incremental： \\\"confirms the categorical finding, but the continuous approach doesn't add substantial new insight\\\"。在median档下被移入appendix。不影响任何core claim但provides defense against \\\"arbitrary cohort split\\\" criticism。\\n\"\n412\t  },\n413\t  {\n414\t    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n415\t    \"description\": \"在architecture-homogeneous子群（decoder-only）上运行DIF，测试去除architecture heterogeneity是否改善IRT fit和减少spurious DIF。\\n\",\n416\t    \"results\": {\n417\t      \"architecture_composition\": {\n418\t        \"total_models\": 5227,\n419\t        \"decoder_only\": 5226,\n420\t        \"non_decoder\": 1,\n421\t        \"pct_decoder_only\": 99.98,\n422\t        \"non_decoder_model\": \"instructor-xl (encoder)\"\n423\t      },\n424\t      \"decoder_only_dif\": {\n425\t        \"c_pct\": 31.3,\n426\t        \"c_pct_change_from_full\": 0.0,\n427\t        \"jaccard_with_full\": 1.0,\n428\t        \"n_flag_changes\": 2\n429\t      },\n430\t      \"irt_fit_comparison\": {\n431\t        \"full_population_rmsea\": 0.052,\n432\t        \"decoder_only_rmsea\": 0.052,\n433\t        \"full_population_cfi\": 0.681,\n434\t        \"decoder_only_cfi\": 0.681,\n435\t        \"fit_change\": \"negligible\"\n436\t      },\n437\t      \"conclusion\": \"Architecture heterogeneity is empirically irrelevant for METABENCH MMLU — population is 99.98% decoder-only\"\n438\t    },\n439\t    \"tables\": [\n440\t      {\n441\t        \"name\": \"Inline: Architecture composition note\",\n442\t        \"content\": \"One sentence in main text: 'METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single encoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0).'\"\n443\t      }\n444\t    ],\n445\t    \"figures\": [],\n446\t    \"analysis\": \"Trivially positive result。在median档下是effective preemptive defense，占用minimal page space。IRT fit的poor numbers（CFI=0.681）需要在limitations中discuss，但 architecture不是原因。\\n\\n\\n这是最clean的\\\"non-issue\\\"实验：METABENCH MMLU几乎entirely decoder-only，移除唯一一个 non-decoder模型对C%和DIF flags毫无影响（Jaccard=1.0）。在median档下，这个result被 reviewers接受为\\\"architecture confound is not a concern for this specific dataset\\\"。 但IRT fit（RMSEA=0.052, CFI=0.681）仍然poor——这不是architecture问题而是MMLU本身的 57-subject multidimensionality。Reviewers接受architecture defense但标注IRT misfit 作为general limitation。在median档下，这个实验在main text用一句话dismiss architecture concern，detail在appendix。\\n\"\n447\t  },\n448\t  {\n449\t    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n450\t    \"description\": \"在real METABENCH response matrix中注入known contamination，测量DIF detection power under controlled ground truth。\\n\",\n451\t    \"results\": {\n452\t      \"temporal_external_matching\": {\n453\t        \"tpr_p0_baseline\": 0.326,\n454\t        \"tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n455\t        \"tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n456\t        \"tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n457\t        \"tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n458\t        \"fpr\": 0.314,\n459\t        \"delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n460\t        \"delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n461\t        \"delta_fpr\": 0.0\n462\t      },\n463\t      \"ability_external_matching\": {\n464\t        \"tpr_p0_baseline\": 0.498,\n465\t        \"tpr_p10\": 0.8,\n466\t        \"fpr\": 0.493,\n467\t        \"delta_tpr_p10\": 0.302\n468\t      },\n469\t      \"within_subject_matching\": {\n470\t        \"fpr_inflation_p10\": \"+0.186\",\n471\t        \"matching_variable_contamination\": true\n472\t      },\n473\t      \"cross_subject_matching\": {\n474\t        \"delta_fpr_all_subjects\": 0.0,\n475\t        \"delta_tpr_cross_gt_within\": \"4/5 subjects\"\n476\t      },\n477\t      \"injection_parameters\": {\n478\t        \"n_clean_items\": 500,\n479\t        \"n_injected_items\": 150,\n480\t        \"exploitation_rates\": [\n481\t          0.0,\n482\t          0.3,\n483\t          0.5,\n484\t          0.7,\n485\t          1.0\n486\t        ],\n487\t        \"focal_group_contaminated\": true\n488\t      }\n489\t    },\n490\t    \"tables\": [\n491\t      {\n492\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Semi-Synthetic Validation Results\",\n493\t        \"content\": \"Matching strategy × injection rate → TPR/FPR/ΔTPR matrix + cross-subject vs within-subject comparison\"\n494\t      }\n495\t    ],\n496\t    \"figures\": [],\n497\t    \"analysis\": \"Claim 3的主要evidence。Median档reviewers接受framework utility但要求更多prior work 对比——\\\"how does this compare to existing semi-synthetic contamination benchmarks (e.g., Oren et al. 2023)?\\\"。Rebuttal需补充2-3个semi-synthetic prior work的 explicit comparison table。ΔFPR=0 across-subject matching是genuine technical contribution但formalization被视为incremental。\\n\\n\\nSemi-synthetic validation是Claim 3的core evidence，在median档下被接受as solid methodological contribution。ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5展示meaningful detection power， cross-subject matching的ΔFPR=0.000是key technical insight。Median档的friction： 1位reviewer指出\\\"the injection mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification that may not reflect real contamination patterns\\\"——real contamination 可能改变response confidence而非binary correctness。这是acknowledged limitation 但不构成rejection reason。Claim 3的\\\"validation framework\\\"contribution被接受， 但Proposition 1的formal proof（ΔFPR=0 algebraic derivation）被1位reviewer称为 \\\"follows straightforwardly from the independence of cross-subject scores and injected items\\\"——即incremental formalization。\\n\"\n498\t  },\n499\t  {\n500\t    \"name\": \"multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\",\n501\t    \"description\": \"在METABENCH中查找additional benchmark response matrices（ARC, HellaSwag, WinoGrande, TruthfulQA），运行temporal DIF分析。\\n\",\n502\t    \"results\": {\n503\t      \"benchmarks\": {\n504\t        \"mmlu\": {\n505\t          \"n_items\": 12508,\n506\t          \"n_ref\": 1080,\n507\t          \"n_foc\": 807,\n508\t          \"pct_c\": 31.3,\n509\t          \"random_pct_c\": 0.18,\n510\t          \"bootstrap_ci\": [\n511\t            29.38,\n512\t            38.05\n513\t          ]\n514\t        },\n515\t        \"winogrande\": {\n516\t          \"n_items\": 1267,\n517\t          \"n_ref\": 1017,\n518\t          \"n_foc\": 803,\n519\t          \"pct_c\": 30.3,\n520\t          \"random_pct_c\": 0.32\n521\t        },\n522\t        \"truthfulqa\": {\n523\t          \"n_items\": 817,\n524\t          \"n_ref\": 1080,\n525\t          \"n_foc\": 807,\n526\t          \"pct_c\": 29.7,\n527\t          \"random_pct_c\": 0.37\n528\t        },\n529\t        \"arc\": {\n530\t          \"n_items\": 1172,\n531\t          \"n_ref\": 1080,\n532\t          \"n_foc\": 807,\n533\t          \"pct_c\": 26.9,\n534\t          \"random_pct_c\": 0.6\n535\t        },\n536\t        \"gsm8k\": {\n537\t          \"n_items\": 1319,\n538\t          \"n_ref\": 1017,\n539\t          \"n_foc\": 804,\n540\t          \"pct_c\": 18.9,\n541\t          \"random_pct_c\": 0.3\n542\t        },\n543\t        \"hellaswag\": {\n544\t          \"n_items\": 10042,\n545\t          \"n_ref\": 1080,\n546\t          \"n_foc\": 807,\n547\t          \"pct_c\": 17.9,\n548\t          \"random_pct_c\": 0.28\n549\t        }\n550\t      },\n551\t      \"summary\": {\n552\t        \"cross_benchmark_range\": \"17.9%–31.3%\",\n553\t        \"all_random_controls_below_1pct\": true,\n554\t        \"min_enrichment_ratio\": 45,\n555\t        \"n_benchmarks\": 6,\n556\t        \"two_tier_pattern\": \"knowledge benchmarks (MMLU/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA/ARC) ≈ 27-31%; skill benchmarks (GSM8K/HellaSwag) ≈ 18-19%\"\n557\t      }\n558\t    },\n559\t    \"tables\": [\n560\t      {\n561\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Cross-Benchmark Temporal DIF\",\n562\t        \"content\": \"6 benchmarks × C% × random control × enrichment ratio\"\n563\t      }\n564\t    ],\n565\t    \"figures\": [],\n566\t    \"analysis\": \"Strong replication evidence。Median档下6-benchmark coverage被接受为\\\"broadest DIF analysis of LLM benchmarks to date\\\"，但HellaSwag/GSM8K的lower C%给reviewer 留下\\\"benchmark-specific\\\"疑虑。Rebuttal需要1段structured argument about why knowledge-heavy vs skill-heavy benchmarks show different DIF rates。这是median档 3-5个rebuttal issues之一。\\n\\n\\n6-benchmark replication是median档下被接受的strength之一。所有benchmarks显示temporal DIF 远高于random control（enrichment ≥45×），证明DIF不是MMLU-specific artifact。但median档的 key friction：HellaSwag和GSM8K的C%显著低于MMLU（17-19% vs 31%），被1-2位reviewers质疑为 \\\"DIF sensitivity may be benchmark-specific — what structural property drives the 2× difference?\\\" 回应需要指向benchmark characteristics：GSM8K是single-domain math，HellaSwag有10K items （statistical dilution），两者的item homogeneity高于MMLU的57-subject heterogeneity。 但这个解释是post-hoc的，reviewer可能不fully satisfied。另外1位reviewer指出 \\\"the two-tier pattern could reflect genuine domain differences in temporal stability rather than methodological artifact\\\"——这实际上strengthens the finding但reviewer frames it as limitation。\\n\"\n567\t  },\n568\t  {\n569\t    \"name\": \"permutation_null_c_rate\",\n570\t    \"description\": \"1000次permutation test：随机重新分配temporal labels（保持N_ref=1080, N_foc=807）， 每次运行MH-DIF，建立C%的null distribution。\\n\",\n571\t    \"results\": {\n572\t      \"n_permutations\": 1000,\n573\t      \"null_distribution\": {\n574\t        \"mean_c_pct\": 0.47,\n575\t        \"sd_c_pct\": 0.13,\n576\t        \"median_c_pct\": 0.45,\n577\t        \"min_c_pct\": 0.1,\n578\t        \"max_c_pct\": 1.02,\n579\t        \"q95_c_pct\": 0.71,\n580\t        \"q99_c_pct\": 0.84\n581\t      },\n582\t      \"observed_c_pct\": 31.3,\n583\t      \"z_score\": 237.2,\n584\t      \"p_value\": \"<0.001 (all 1000 permutations below observed)\",\n585\t      \"empirical_p\": 0.0,\n586\t      \"effect_size_ratio\": \"observed/null_mean = 66.6×\",\n587\t      \"per_family_stratified\": {\n588\t        \"status\": \"not executed pre-submission\",\n589\t        \"rationale\": \"identified as potential rebuttal experiment; requires grouping models by family and permuting within strata\",\n590\t        \"estimated_null_mean_if_stratified\": 0.52,\n591\t        \"estimated_z_if_stratified\": \">200\"\n592\t      }\n593\t    },\n594\t    \"tables\": [\n595\t      {\n596\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Permutation Null Distribution\",\n597\t        \"content\": \"Null C% summary statistics + observed vs null comparison + z-score + empirical p\"\n598\t      }\n599\t    ],\n600\t    \"figures\": [],\n601\t    \"analysis\": \"Statistically unambiguous result。Median档reviewers接受statistical significance 但push for stronger controls（per-family stratification）。这是well-targeted reviewer request——the paper should preemptively address it using plan_022 de-duplication as evidence that family structure doesn't inflate C%, and offer stratified permutation as rebuttal experiment if needed。在median档下，plan_029成功但creates a follow-up obligation in rebuttal。\\n\\n\\nPermutation null在median档下成功确认31.3%远超chance（p<0.001, z>200）。Null distribution 的mean C%=0.47%与within-cohort random split的0.18%在同一量级，内部一致。这直接回应 \\\"is 31% above chance?\\\"质疑。但median档的nuance：1位reviewer接受permutation null但 要求additional controls——specifically per-family stratified permutation，因为如果 model families cluster by temporal cohort（2023多Llama-2，2024多Llama-3），简单 permutation可能underestimate null。这成为rebuttal experiment需求。Plan_022的 de-duplication分析（K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%）provides partial defense，但 reviewer要求的是stratified permutation而非cap-based de-duplication。这是median档 3-5个rebuttal issues之一。\\n\"\n602\t  },\n603\t  {\n604\t    \"name\": \"odds_ratio_regression_transparency\",\n605\t    \"description\": \"补充pseudo R²=0.0007的透明度：odds ratio + 95% CI + McFadden/Nagelkerke R² + deviance ratio。增加item-level accuracy change predictor。\\n\",\n606\t    \"results\": {\n607\t      \"model1_domain_delta\": {\n608\t        \"predictor\": \"subject-level accuracy change (2024-2023)\",\n609\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0007,\n610\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0012,\n611\t        \"aic\": 15545.2,\n612\t        \"or_per_010_acc_change\": 1.55,\n613\t        \"or_ci_per_010\": [\n614\t          1.19,\n615\t          2.03\n616\t        ],\n617\t        \"interpretation\": \"10pp domain improvement → 1.55× odds of DIF, but explains <0.2% variance\"\n618\t      },\n619\t      \"model2_domain_plus_items\": {\n620\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0423,\n621\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.072,\n622\t        \"aic\": 14902.3,\n623\t        \"domain_delta_or\": 0.73,\n624\t        \"ctt_difficulty_or\": 0.78,\n625\t        \"ctt_discrimination_or\": 1.51,\n626\t        \"simpsons_paradox\": true,\n627\t        \"interpretation\": \"Domain accuracy delta REVERSES direction after controlling for item properties — Simpson's paradox\"\n628\t      },\n629\t      \"model3_item_delta\": {\n630\t        \"predictor\": \"item-level accuracy change (per-item 2024-2023 delta)\",\n631\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0012,\n632\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0021,\n633\t        \"aic\": 15536.9,\n634\t        \"item_acc_change_or_per_010\": 1.08,\n635\t        \"item_acc_change_ci\": [\n636\t          1.51,\n637\t          2.96\n638\t        ]\n639\t      },\n640\t      \"model4_full\": {\n641\t        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0434,\n642\t        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0737,\n643\t        \"aic\": 14885.4,\n644\t        \"item_delta_or\": 0.92,\n645\t        \"difficulty_or\": 0.77,\n646\t        \"discrimination_or\": 1.54,\n647\t        \"lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2\": 655.53\n648\t      },\n649\t      \"simpsons_paradox_narrative\": \"\\\"Domain improvement predicts DIF marginally (OR=1.55), but this relationship REVERSES (OR=0.73) after controlling for item difficulty and discrimination. Items that are harder and more discriminating are more likely to show DIF, regardless of domain-level improvement. The 'models got better' story is a Simpson's paradox — improvement concentrates in domains with harder, more discriminating items.\\\"\\n\"\n650\t    },\n651\t    \"tables\": [\n652\t      {\n653\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Logistic Regression Decomposition\",\n654\t        \"content\": \"4 models: domain Δ only → domain Δ + items → item Δ only → item Δ + items; OR, CI, R², AIC for each\"\n655\t      }\n656\t    ],\n657\t    \"figures\": [],\n658\t    \"analysis\": \"Key analytical contribution。在median档下Simpson's paradox被视为paper的most surprising finding之一，多数reviewers find it compelling。但endogeneity concern prevents full resolution of \\\"why 31%?\\\"——paper需honestly position这as \\\"DIF is predominantly item-specific, not domain-driven, but the causal direction between item properties and DIF remains ambiguous\\\"。这contributes to causal language hedging requirement。\\n\\nSimpson's paradox是median档下的strong defense line。Domain-level accuracy improvement 与DIF的marginal association（OR=1.55, R²<0.002）在控制item properties后reverses （OR=0.73），证明\\\"models got better\\\"不是DIF的driver——item difficulty和discrimination 才是。在median档下，这个result被2位reviewers接受为convincing decomposition evidence。 但1位reviewer质疑：\\\"item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — DIF items are harder BECAUSE they function differently across cohorts, not vice versa\\\"。 这是valid methodological point，paper需在limitations中acknowledge endogeneity concern。 Simpson's paradox被用在rebuttal中作为\\\"second line of defense\\\"（与plan_027 ability overlap d=-0.17并用）回应\\\"31% is just capability improvement\\\"质疑。\\n\"\n659\t  }\n660\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68384416-f199-481e-b490-5f37e9ab5fc0","uuid":"996375c3-76b0-4c04-b33a-b818272f60d7","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:46:02.034Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T141728/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n    \"description\": \"对METABENCH MMLU响应矩阵（5219模型×12508题目）进行MH-DIF分析。包括temporal cohort split (2023 vs 2024-H1)、ability-quintile split、within-family confound control (Llama-2 vs Llama-3)、domain-specificity分析、Li et al. web-overlap proxy验证。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_cohort\": {\n        \"n_ref\": 1080,\n        \"n_foc\": 807,\n        \"ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n        \"ets_b_pct\": 20.5,\n        \"ets_a_pct\": 48.2,\n        \"mean_delta_mh_c_items\": 2.14,\n        \"median_delta_mh_c_items\": 1.78\n      },\n      \"ability_cohort\": {\n        \"ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n        \"enrichment\": 1.19\n      },\n      \"within_family\": {\n        \"llama2_vs_llama3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n        \"mistral_vs_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n        \"llama_jaccard_with_temporal\": 0.28\n      },\n      \"domain_specificity\": {\n        \"spearman_rho_acc_improvement_vs_c_pct\": 0.307,\n        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n        \"n_subjects\": 57,\n        \"all_subjects_have_dif\": true,\n        \"c_pct_range\": [\n          20.7,\n          48.4\n        ]\n      },\n      \"proxy_validation\": {\n        \"li_et_al_coverage\": 0.738,\n        \"enrichment_temporal\": 0.96,\n        \"fpr_li_clean_temporal\": 0.318,\n        \"enrichment_ability\": 1.19,\n        \"fpr_li_clean_ability\": 0.027\n      },\n      \"sanity_check\": {\n        \"random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n        \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"4-way sensitivity matrix: cohort × item filtering → C% values\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Domain-Specificity\",\n        \"content\": \"57 subjects × C% × accuracy improvement correlation\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心结果solid。Median档reviewers的主要friction点：(1) within-family Llama-2v3的C%=61.3% 远高于temporal 31.3%，需要解释为什么family comparison不是更好的design；(2) domain ρ=0.307 虽然p=0.02但effect size modest，需要plan_019 item-level decomposition作为补充； (3) Li et al. proxy validation的\\\"negative result\\\"需要更清晰的framing——是validation failure 还是expected orthogonality。8页压缩下within-family detail可能被移入appendix。\\n\\n\\n在median档位下，31.3% C%是核心发现，被Claim 1直接支撑。Reviewers接受这个数字的statistical significance（random split仅0.18%），但至少1位reviewer要求更强的causal language hedging—— 因为within-family分析（Llama-2 vs Llama-3 C%=61.3%）显示family-level capability jump也会 产生高DIF，temporal cohort的31.3%可能混合了genuine item instability和capability-driven DIF。 ρ=0.307的domain-level correlation被接受为modest ecological correlation，但reviewer要求 明确\\\"item-level decomposition shows only 2.4pp explained\\\"（来自plan_019/030）。 Enrichment≈0.96支撑Claim 2但被1位reviewer视为\\\"expected by construction\\\"。Ability cohort 的2.9% C%作为negative control被接受。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"验证DIF对reasoning-RL模型的鲁棒性。从METABENCH筛选alignment-RL模型（DPO/ORPO，N≈477）， 外加10-15个open-weight reasoning-RL模型（GRPO/PPO），测试DIF检测稳定性并与传统检测器对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alignment_rl_cohort\": {\n        \"n_models\": 477,\n        \"c_pct_with_alignment_rl\": 31.1,\n        \"c_pct_without\": 31.3,\n        \"jaccard_flags_overlap\": 0.968,\n        \"flag_stability\": \"negligible change\"\n      },\n      \"reasoning_rl_models\": {\n        \"n_available\": 13,\n        \"models_tested\": [\n          \"deepseek-r1-7b\",\n          \"deepseek-r1-32b\",\n          \"qwen2.5-rl-7b\",\n          \"qwen2.5-rl-14b\",\n          \"qwen2.5-rl-32b\",\n          \"o1-mini-proxy\",\n          \"skywork-or1-8b\",\n          \"open-reasoner-7b\",\n          \"marco-o1-7b\",\n          \"k2-65b\",\n          \"rstar-math-7b\",\n          \"still-2-1.5b\",\n          \"llemma-rl-7b\"\n        ],\n        \"c_pct_with_rl_in_focal\": 31.0,\n        \"c_pct_change\": -0.3,\n        \"jaccard_with_vs_without_rl\": 0.971\n      },\n      \"traditional_detector_comparison\": {\n        \"mink_auroc_non_rl\": 0.714,\n        \"mink_auroc_rl_models\": 0.528,\n        \"mink_auroc_delta\": -0.186,\n        \"constat_auroc_non_rl\": 0.681,\n        \"constat_auroc_rl_models\": 0.513,\n        \"constat_auroc_delta\": -0.168,\n        \"dif_retention_ratio\": 0.987\n      },\n      \"statistical_tests\": {\n        \"delong_mink_p\": 0.089,\n        \"delong_constat_p\": 0.112,\n        \"tost_equivalence\": \"inconclusive (CI: [-0.04, 0.07], bounds ±0.10)\",\n        \"bootstrap_ci_dif_retention\": [\n          0.93,\n          1.03\n        ]\n      },\n      \"power_analysis\": {\n        \"partial_exploitation_p04\": \"delta_MH≈0.84, TPR≈0.31\",\n        \"partial_exploitation_p07\": \"delta_MH≈1.18, TPR≈0.52\",\n        \"partial_exploitation_p10\": \"delta_MH≈1.68, TPR≈0.76\",\n        \"detection_boundary\": \"p≈0.55 for TPR≥0.50 at N=100\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S1 (Appendix): RL Robustness Comparison\",\n        \"content\": \"AUROC comparison across DIF/Min-K%/ConStat × model type (non-RL, alignment-RL, reasoning-RL)\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"N=13是致命弱点。实验方向正确但statistical power不足以支撑numbered claim。 Median档策略：在limitations中honest disclosure \\\"reasoning-RL robustness remains an open question due to limited open-weight availability\\\"，同时在main text保留 alignment-RL的positive result（N=477，C% stable at 31.1%）作为partial evidence。 Reviewer不会因此reject但会在score中扣分（contributes to 3.25-3.75 range）。\\n\\n\\nMedian档位的关键限制：reasoning-RL模型仅13个，远低于统计显著性所需的样本量。DIF是group-level 方法，将13个RL模型混入N≈807的focal cohort几乎不改变C%（31.3%→31.0%），但这也意味着无法 单独评估RL模型的DIF特性。传统检测器（Min-K%，ConStat）在RL模型上的AUROC下降（0.71→0.53, 0.68→0.51），方向支持\\\"DIF比per-model方法更robust\\\"的claim，但DeLong test p>0.05因为N=13 power不足。TOST等价性检验inconclusive——CI包含零但也包含meaningful differences。 在median档下，这个实验被降级到Limitations section作为\\\"directional evidence\\\"， reviewers接受reasoning-RL是emerging phenomenon、数据有限的framing，但1位reviewer 标注\\\"this weakens the practical relevance claim for post-2024 models\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"独立评估ConStat-style perturbation testing在MMLU上的检测力。需要GPU生成语义等价 reformulations并收集模型响应。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n      \"reason\": \"GPU budget constraint (80h required) + 依赖LLM paraphrasing pipeline未搭建\",\n      \"counterfactual_if_executed\": {\n        \"n_items_reformulated\": 250,\n        \"constat_fdr_controlled_detection_rate\": 0.42,\n        \"constat_auroc_non_rl\": 0.68,\n        \"constat_auroc_rl\": 0.51,\n        \"constat_dif_overlap_jaccard\": 0.18,\n        \"constat_specificity\": \"high for verbatim contamination, low for capability-driven DIF\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"未执行。对median档outcome的影响：1位reviewer在minor comments中提到\\\"direct comparison with ConStat would strengthen the paper\\\"，但接受conceptual distinction argument。 不是core weakness。\\n\\n\\n在median档位下，plan_003a未执行是合理的——paper已pivot away from ensemble detection (Claim 2 old) toward diagnostic framing。GPU预算优先分配给plan_002和plan_004。 ConStat/DVD的AUROC数字已通过文献引用在main text中提供（Blebea et al. 2024）， 无需独立复现。Reviewers可能要求\\\"why not compare directly\\\"但rebuttal可以指向 ConStat的public results + 不同detection targets（perturbation sensitivity vs differential functioning）的conceptual argument。在median档下这不构成reject reason 但contributes to \\\"thin empirical comparison\\\" concern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"独立评估DVD generation variance在MMLU上的检测力。需要GPU对10-15个模型生成50次响应。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n      \"reason\": \"GPU budget constraint (70h required) + 需要open-weight model inference pipeline\",\n      \"counterfactual_if_executed\": {\n        \"n_models\": 12,\n        \"responses_per_item\": 50,\n        \"dvd_detection_rate\": 0.35,\n        \"dvd_auroc\": 0.62,\n        \"dvd_variant_contamination_sensitivity\": 0.71,\n        \"dvd_verbatim_contamination_sensitivity\": 0.44\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"未执行。影响与plan_003a类似，合并为一个reviewer concern：\\\"existing method comparison is conceptual rather than empirical\\\"。Median档下这是minor issue，不影响accept/reject。\\n\\n\\n与plan_003a相同逻辑——paper不再追求ensemble detection，DVD作为independent baseline 的value在current framing下降低。Median档reviewers理解GPU constraint但可能在 \\\"comparison with existing methods\\\" section标注insufficiency。Rebuttal中可指向 DVD原始论文结果 + \\\"DIF operates at group level while DVD operates at model level, complementary rather than competing\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n    \"description\": \"融合DIF + ConStat + DVD为多信号ensemble。依赖plan_003a和plan_003b。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n      \"reason\": \"Dependencies plan_003a and plan_003b not executed; ensemble claim dropped from paper\",\n      \"paper_status\": \"Dropped to future work section\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"完全dropped。无直接影响，但间接加剧Claim 4 actionability的weakness——如果ensemble 存在，actionability story会更强。Median档下这是background weakness，不是explicit reviewer complaint。\\n\\n\\nPlan_003c在paper pivot后被完全dropped。Paper从\\\"we detect contamination better via ensemble\\\"转向\\\"we characterize benchmark properties via DIF\\\"。Median档reviewers 不会miss这个experiment因为paper不再claim ensemble contribution。但1位reviewer 可能在\\\"future work\\\"评论中写\\\"the ensemble direction seems promising and its absence weakens the practical impact\\\"——这contributes to actionability concern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n    \"description\": \"在GSM8K上复现DIF分析，使用GSM1K作为contamination ground truth。包括temporal DIF、 semi-synthetic validation、GSM1K correlation三步。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"step1_temporal_dif\": {\n        \"n_items\": 1319,\n        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n        \"n_foc\": 804,\n        \"standard_c_pct\": 18.9,\n        \"external_c_pct\": 47.4,\n        \"sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n        \"standard_external_spearman\": 0.926\n      },\n      \"step2_semi_synthetic\": {\n        \"standard_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n        \"standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n        \"external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n        \"fpr_stable\": true\n      },\n      \"step3_gsm1k_correlation\": {\n        \"n_matched_models\": 33,\n        \"pearson_r\": -0.478,\n        \"pearson_p\": 0.005,\n        \"spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n        \"partial_r_controlling_accuracy\": -0.385,\n        \"partial_p\": 0.027,\n        \"direction\": \"NEGATIVE — opposite to naive contamination hypothesis\",\n        \"interpretation\": \"DIF-C items ANTI-correlate with contamination gap; DIF captures capability differential, not contamination per se\",\n        \"ci_95_pearson\": [\n          -0.71,\n          -0.16\n        ],\n        \"ci_95_spearman\": [\n          -0.66,\n          -0.03\n        ],\n        \"cook_d_max\": \"deepseek-math-7b-rl\",\n        \"leave_one_out_robust\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Cross-Benchmark DIF Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"GSM8K temporal DIF: C%=18.9%, ΔTPR=+0.818, GSM1K r=-0.478\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mixed result。Semi-synthetic validation强化Claim 3，但GSM1K negative correlation + lower C%创造了tension。Median档reviewers接受\\\"DIF captures differential functioning broadly, not just contamination\\\"的framing，但GSM1K result被从abstract/conclusion 移除。HellaSwag C%=17.9%（来自plan_028）进一步支持\\\"lower rates on non-MMLU benchmarks\\\" 的pattern，给reviewer ammunition质疑MMLU-specificity。\\n\\n\\nGSM8K的C%=18.9%显著低于MMLU的31.3%，在median档下被1位reviewer质疑为\\\"DIF may be benchmark-specific — lower rates on math benchmarks suggest the phenomenon is modulated by domain characteristics\\\"。这是valid concern因为GSM8K是单领域数学题， item homogeneity高于MMLU的57-subject结构。GSM1K correlation的r=-0.478方向为负 （与contamination hypothesis相反），被demoted to exploratory per Dream #6 consensus。 N=33 + wide CI [-0.71, -0.16]使这个结果在median档下不被视为strong evidence。 Semi-synthetic ΔTPR=+0.818则是positive result，支撑Claim 3的framework portability。 Median档下Step 2被接受，Step 3被标注\\\"exploratory, underpowered\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"在MMLU上拟合bifactor IRT模型（general factor + 57 subject-specific factors），选择 anchor items进行fixed-parameter calibration equating。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"attempted_and_killed\",\n      \"convergence\": {\n        \"full_57_subject\": \"failed to converge after 5000 EM iterations\",\n        \"reduced_10_subject\": \"converged but poor fit\",\n        \"reduced_5_subject\": \"converged, marginal fit\"\n      },\n      \"fit_statistics_5_subject\": {\n        \"rmsea\": 0.078,\n        \"cfi\": 0.724,\n        \"tli\": 0.698,\n        \"srmr\": 0.091\n      },\n      \"anchor_item_selection\": {\n        \"n_candidate_anchors\": 312,\n        \"anchor_stability_criterion\": \"DIF A-class + discrimination > 0.8\",\n        \"anchor_coverage\": \"38/57 subjects represented\"\n      },\n      \"equating_pilot\": {\n        \"status\": \"abandoned — fit insufficient for reliable equating\",\n        \"rho_equated_vs_original\": null,\n        \"decision\": \"killed; within-subject DIF (plan_014) provides alternative without requiring full IRT model\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Expected failure。在median档下被移入limitations section作为\\\"our attempts to improve IRT model specification did not succeed, but within-subject validation (plan_014) confirms DIF findings are not artifacts of cross-subject matching\\\"。Contributes to the \\\"three structural constraints\\\" narrative。不直接影响reviewer score。\\n\\n\\nBifactor IRT在MMLU上失败是structurally predictable的：57个subjects × 12508 items的 bifactor model需要估计~57 specific factors + 1 general factor + ~25000 item parameters， 计算上不可行且psychometrically questionable（MMLU的57 subjects不是designed dimensions）。 在median档下，这个failure被report为\\\"empirical observation that motivates future multidimensional IRT work\\\"，positioned as honest negative result。Plan_014的 within-subject DIF（C%=38.1%）提供了alternative path证明DIF不依赖于cross-subject matching artifact。Reviewer可能质疑\\\"why attempt bifactor at all\\\"但不会因failure 扣分——negative results是legitimate contribution if honestly reported。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"为DIF-flagged MMLU items生成替换题目，通过student simulation进行difficulty calibration。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"blocked\",\n      \"blocking_dependency\": \"plan_005 (bifactor IRT) killed — no equating framework for calibration\",\n      \"alternative_path\": \"plan_032 DIF-cleaned demonstration provides actionability evidence without item replacement\",\n      \"counterfactual_if_executed\": {\n        \"n_items_generated\": 500,\n        \"difficulty_correlation_prompt\": 0.32,\n        \"difficulty_correlation_simulation\": 0.71,\n        \"construct_fidelity_human_eval\": 0.64,\n        \"replacement_set_rho_vs_original\": 0.989\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Blocked。Paper已完全pivot away from regeneration claim。在median档下无影响。\\n\\n\\nPlan_006被plan_005 failure阻塞是合理的——没有可靠的IRT equating framework， replacement items无法calibrated到同一量表上。在median档下，paper不claim \\\"benchmark regeneration\\\"（已从original framing dropped），改为claim \\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"。Plan_032的DIF-cleaned demonstration（89.5% models shift ≥5 ranks, z=8.5 vs random）提供了不需要item replacement的actionability evidence。Reviewers不会miss这个experiment因为paper不再promise regeneration。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"实现Sinharay et al. (2006)的cumulative Bayesian DIF priors，模拟4次连续benchmark administrations，展示累积evidence带来的power improvement。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"simulation_design\": {\n        \"n_administrations\": 4,\n        \"n_items_per_admin\": 500,\n        \"n_models_per_admin\": 200,\n        \"effect_sizes\": [\n          0.8,\n          1.0,\n          1.2,\n          1.4,\n          1.6\n        ],\n        \"contamination_prevalence\": 0.15\n      },\n      \"power_results\": {\n        \"single_admin_tpr_d10\": 0.397,\n        \"cumulative_2_admin_tpr_d10\": 0.548,\n        \"cumulative_3_admin_tpr_d10\": 0.681,\n        \"cumulative_4_admin_tpr_d10\": 0.739,\n        \"single_admin_tpr_d14\": 0.682,\n        \"cumulative_3_admin_tpr_d14\": 0.841\n      },\n      \"fpr_all_conditions\": \"<0.06\",\n      \"prior_weight_sensitivity\": {\n        \"informative_prior_tpr_3admin\": 0.681,\n        \"flat_prior_tpr_3admin\": 0.523,\n        \"prior_impact\": \"+0.158 TPR from informative priors\"\n      },\n      \"bayes_factor_threshold\": {\n        \"bf_gt_3_pct_3admin\": 0.58,\n        \"bf_gt_10_pct_3admin\": 0.41\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S2 (Appendix): Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power\",\n        \"content\": \"TPR × n_administrations × effect_size matrix + BF threshold analysis\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Simulation-only结果在median档下被视为supplementary。主要value是为Discussion中 \\\"longitudinal benchmark monitoring protocol\\\"提供quantitative grounding。 不直接影响reviewer score但strengthens the \\\"audit protocol\\\" narrative for Claim 4。\\n\\n\\nCumulative Bayesian DIF在simulation中表现符合预期：3次administration后power从0.40 提升到0.68（δ=1.0），符合Sinharay et al.的理论预测。但这是pure simulation——没有在 real METABENCH data上进行temporal sliding window validation。在median档下， 这个experiment被放入appendix作为\\\"methodological extension for longitudinal benchmark monitoring\\\"。Reviewers将其视为incremental：1位reviewer写\\\"the Bayesian accumulation is a known technique; the contribution here is applying it to the LLM context, which is straightforward\\\"。Proposition 1的formal proof（cross-subject ΔFPR=0） 被同一位reviewer称为\\\"incremental\\\"——这两个方法贡献合并被视为不够novel。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析benchmark在progressive item replacement下的validity degradation。模拟5%-50% replacement rate，测量ranking stability、score reliability、construct coverage。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"replacement_rates\": [\n        0.05,\n        0.1,\n        0.15,\n        0.2,\n        0.3,\n        0.5\n      ],\n      \"ranking_stability_rho\": {\n        \"pct_05\": 0.9994,\n        \"pct_10\": 0.9981,\n        \"pct_15\": 0.9963,\n        \"pct_20\": 0.9938,\n        \"pct_30\": 0.9867,\n        \"pct_50\": 0.9714\n      },\n      \"score_reliability_alpha\": {\n        \"original\": 0.962,\n        \"pct_05\": 0.959,\n        \"pct_10\": 0.955,\n        \"pct_15\": 0.95,\n        \"pct_20\": 0.944,\n        \"pct_30\": 0.929,\n        \"pct_50\": 0.898\n      },\n      \"construct_coverage\": {\n        \"pct_subjects_ge80pct_items_at_20pct\": 0.947,\n        \"pct_subjects_ge80pct_items_at_50pct\": 0.614,\n        \"first_subject_below_80pct\": \"formal_logic (N=126, loses >25 items at 20%)\"\n      },\n      \"theoretical_bound\": {\n        \"rho_lower_bound_at_r\": \"ρ ≥ 1 - r × (1 - α_replacement) / α_original, approximate\",\n        \"validity_threshold\": \"ρ < 0.99 at ~22% replacement for MMLU\"\n      },\n      \"comparison_with_plan_032\": {\n        \"plan_032_rho\": 0.9965,\n        \"graceful_degradation_predicted_rho_at_31pct\": 0.9856,\n        \"discrepancy\": \"DIF-targeted removal is LESS disruptive than random replacement (0.9965 > 0.9856), consistent with plan_020 circularity ablation\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S3 (Appendix): Graceful Degradation Metrics\",\n        \"content\": \"Replacement rate × ρ × α × construct coverage matrix\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Clean supplementary result。在median档下strengthens \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative但simultaneously feeds reviewer skepticism about practical significance。 这是median档的核心tension：数据越是显示ranking robustness，actionability argument 越难卖。\\n\\n\\nGraceful degradation分析在median档下支撑\\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\"叙事：即使移除31% items，ρ仍>0.98（random replacement）或>0.996（DIF-targeted removal）。这与plan_017 的ρ=0.997一致。但reviewer的tension点恰恰在这里：\\\"if benchmark is this redundant, what's the practical value of identifying unstable items?\\\"至少1位reviewer质疑 actionability——31% items unstable but rankings barely change，所以who cares？ Plan_032的cohort asymmetry（2024 Δrank=+73.6）是回应这个质疑的ammunition，但 在median档下论证力度不够——reviewer要求control for model quality confound。 Graceful degradation本身被接受为clean supplementary analysis但被移入appendix。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n    \"description\": \"实现Tutz & Berger (2016) Item-Focused Trees作为categorical DIF的alternative， 将model release date作为continuous covariate。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model\": {\n        \"splitting_variable\": \"release_date (continuous, days since 2023-01-01)\",\n        \"tree_depth\": 3,\n        \"n_terminal_nodes\": 5,\n        \"primary_split\": \"2023-08-15 (separating early-2023 from late-2023+)\",\n        \"secondary_split\": \"2024-02-01 (within late-2023+ group)\"\n      },\n      \"dif_detection\": {\n        \"n_items_significant\": 3421,\n        \"pct_items_significant\": 27.4,\n        \"overlap_with_mh_c\": 0.823,\n        \"jaccard_with_mh_c\": 0.691,\n        \"items_only_ift\": 487,\n        \"items_only_mh\": 984\n      },\n      \"temporal_gradient\": {\n        \"effect_size_vs_time_distance_r\": 0.312,\n        \"effect_size_vs_time_distance_p\": \"<0.001\",\n        \"early_2023_vs_late_2024_mean_dif\": 1.87,\n        \"adjacent_half_years_mean_dif\": 0.94\n      },\n      \"model_fit\": {\n        \"deviance_explained_r2\": 0.031,\n        \"aic_vs_categorical\": \"IFT AIC=48921 vs MH-categorical AIC=49103 (marginal improvement)\"\n      },\n      \"conclusion\": \"IFT confirms temporal gradient but adds limited explanatory power beyond categorical MH\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S4 (Appendix): IFT vs MH-DIF Comparison\",\n        \"content\": \"Item overlap, detection rates, split points\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Supplementary robustness check。Median档下reviewers不explicitly request这个分析 但它preemptively addresses \\\"arbitrary cohort boundary\\\" concern。Value在于showing temporal DIF是gradient而非artifact of specific cutoff。被appendix化对page budget 有利。\\n\\n\\nIFT在median档下是\\\"nice to have\\\"的robustness check。与MH-DIF的82.3% overlap确认 categorical temporal split不是arbitrary——continuous analysis recovers similar items。 Primary split at ~2023-08-15大致对应LLM rapid improvement期（Llama-2 release附近）， 但R²=0.031说明release date alone解释DIF variation极少。Reviewer视为incremental： \\\"confirms the categorical finding, but the continuous approach doesn't add substantial new insight\\\"。在median档下被移入appendix。不影响任何core claim但provides defense against \\\"arbitrary cohort split\\\" criticism。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"在architecture-homogeneous子群（decoder-only）上运行DIF，测试去除architecture heterogeneity是否改善IRT fit和减少spurious DIF。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"architecture_composition\": {\n        \"total_models\": 5227,\n        \"decoder_only\": 5226,\n        \"non_decoder\": 1,\n        \"pct_decoder_only\": 99.98,\n        \"non_decoder_model\": \"instructor-xl (encoder)\"\n      },\n      \"decoder_only_dif\": {\n        \"c_pct\": 31.3,\n        \"c_pct_change_from_full\": 0.0,\n        \"jaccard_with_full\": 1.0,\n        \"n_flag_changes\": 2\n      },\n      \"irt_fit_comparison\": {\n        \"full_population_rmsea\": 0.052,\n        \"decoder_only_rmsea\": 0.052,\n        \"full_population_cfi\": 0.681,\n        \"decoder_only_cfi\": 0.681,\n        \"fit_change\": \"negligible\"\n      },\n      \"conclusion\": \"Architecture heterogeneity is empirically irrelevant for METABENCH MMLU — population is 99.98% decoder-only\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Inline: Architecture composition note\",\n        \"content\": \"One sentence in main text: 'METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single encoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0).'\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Trivially positive result。在median档下是effective preemptive defense，占用minimal page space。IRT fit的poor numbers（CFI=0.681）需要在limitations中discuss，但 architecture不是原因。\\n\\n\\n这是最clean的\\\"non-issue\\\"实验：METABENCH MMLU几乎entirely decoder-only，移除唯一一个 non-decoder模型对C%和DIF flags毫无影响（Jaccard=1.0）。在median档下，这个result被 reviewers接受为\\\"architecture confound is not a concern for this specific dataset\\\"。 但IRT fit（RMSEA=0.052, CFI=0.681）仍然poor——这不是architecture问题而是MMLU本身的 57-subject multidimensionality。Reviewers接受architecture defense但标注IRT misfit 作为general limitation。在median档下，这个实验在main text用一句话dismiss architecture concern，detail在appendix。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"在real METABENCH response matrix中注入known contamination，测量DIF detection power under controlled ground truth。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_external_matching\": {\n        \"tpr_p0_baseline\": 0.326,\n        \"tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n        \"tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n        \"tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n        \"tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n        \"fpr\": 0.314,\n        \"delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n        \"delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n        \"delta_fpr\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"ability_external_matching\": {\n        \"tpr_p0_baseline\": 0.498,\n        \"tpr_p10\": 0.8,\n        \"fpr\": 0.493,\n        \"delta_tpr_p10\": 0.302\n      },\n      \"within_subject_matching\": {\n        \"fpr_inflation_p10\": \"+0.186\",\n        \"matching_variable_contamination\": true\n      },\n      \"cross_subject_matching\": {\n        \"delta_fpr_all_subjects\": 0.0,\n        \"delta_tpr_cross_gt_within\": \"4/5 subjects\"\n      },\n      \"injection_parameters\": {\n        \"n_clean_items\": 500,\n        \"n_injected_items\": 150,\n        \"exploitation_rates\": [\n          0.0,\n          0.3,\n          0.5,\n          0.7,\n          1.0\n        ],\n        \"focal_group_contaminated\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Semi-Synthetic Validation Results\",\n        \"content\": \"Matching strategy × injection rate → TPR/FPR/ΔTPR matrix + cross-subject vs within-subject comparison\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Claim 3的主要evidence。Median档reviewers接受framework utility但要求更多prior work 对比——\\\"how does this compare to existing semi-synthetic contamination benchmarks (e.g., Oren et al. 2023)?\\\"。Rebuttal需补充2-3个semi-synthetic prior work的 explicit comparison table。ΔFPR=0 across-subject matching是genuine technical contribution但formalization被视为incremental。\\n\\n\\nSemi-synthetic validation是Claim 3的core evidence，在median档下被接受as solid methodological contribution。ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5展示meaningful detection power， cross-subject matching的ΔFPR=0.000是key technical insight。Median档的friction： 1位reviewer指出\\\"the injection mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification that may not reflect real contamination patterns\\\"——real contamination 可能改变response confidence而非binary correctness。这是acknowledged limitation 但不构成rejection reason。Claim 3的\\\"validation framework\\\"contribution被接受， 但Proposition 1的formal proof（ΔFPR=0 algebraic derivation）被1位reviewer称为 \\\"follows straightforwardly from the independence of cross-subject scores and injected items\\\"——即incremental formalization。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"在METABENCH中查找additional benchmark response matrices（ARC, HellaSwag, WinoGrande, TruthfulQA），运行temporal DIF分析。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"benchmarks\": {\n        \"mmlu\": {\n          \"n_items\": 12508,\n          \"n_ref\": 1080,\n          \"n_foc\": 807,\n          \"pct_c\": 31.3,\n          \"random_pct_c\": 0.18,\n          \"bootstrap_ci\": [\n            29.38,\n            38.05\n          ]\n        },\n        \"winogrande\": {\n          \"n_items\": 1267,\n          \"n_ref\": 1017,\n          \"n_foc\": 803,\n          \"pct_c\": 30.3,\n          \"random_pct_c\": 0.32\n        },\n        \"truthfulqa\": {\n          \"n_items\": 817,\n          \"n_ref\": 1080,\n          \"n_foc\": 807,\n          \"pct_c\": 29.7,\n          \"random_pct_c\": 0.37\n        },\n        \"arc\": {\n          \"n_items\": 1172,\n          \"n_ref\": 1080,\n          \"n_foc\": 807,\n          \"pct_c\": 26.9,\n          \"random_pct_c\": 0.6\n        },\n        \"gsm8k\": {\n          \"n_items\": 1319,\n          \"n_ref\": 1017,\n          \"n_foc\": 804,\n          \"pct_c\": 18.9,\n          \"random_pct_c\": 0.3\n        },\n        \"hellaswag\": {\n          \"n_items\": 10042,\n          \"n_ref\": 1080,\n          \"n_foc\": 807,\n          \"pct_c\": 17.9,\n          \"random_pct_c\": 0.28\n        }\n      },\n      \"summary\": {\n        \"cross_benchmark_range\": \"17.9%–31.3%\",\n        \"all_random_controls_below_1pct\": true,\n        \"min_enrichment_ratio\": 45,\n        \"n_benchmarks\": 6,\n        \"two_tier_pattern\": \"knowledge benchmarks (MMLU/WinoGrande/TruthfulQA/ARC) ≈ 27-31%; skill benchmarks (GSM8K/HellaSwag) ≈ 18-19%\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Cross-Benchmark Temporal DIF\",\n        \"content\": \"6 benchmarks × C% × random control × enrichment ratio\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Strong replication evidence。Median档下6-benchmark coverage被接受为\\\"broadest DIF analysis of LLM benchmarks to date\\\"，但HellaSwag/GSM8K的lower C%给reviewer 留下\\\"benchmark-specific\\\"疑虑。Rebuttal需要1段structured argument about why knowledge-heavy vs skill-heavy benchmarks show different DIF rates。这是median档 3-5个rebuttal issues之一。\\n\\n\\n6-benchmark replication是median档下被接受的strength之一。所有benchmarks显示temporal DIF 远高于random control（enrichment ≥45×），证明DIF不是MMLU-specific artifact。但median档的 key friction：HellaSwag和GSM8K的C%显著低于MMLU（17-19% vs 31%），被1-2位reviewers质疑为 \\\"DIF sensitivity may be benchmark-specific — what structural property drives the 2× difference?\\\" 回应需要指向benchmark characteristics：GSM8K是single-domain math，HellaSwag有10K items （statistical dilution），两者的item homogeneity高于MMLU的57-subject heterogeneity。 但这个解释是post-hoc的，reviewer可能不fully satisfied。另外1位reviewer指出 \\\"the two-tier pattern could reflect genuine domain differences in temporal stability rather than methodological artifact\\\"——这实际上strengthens the finding但reviewer frames it as limitation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"permutation_null_c_rate\",\n    \"description\": \"1000次permutation test：随机重新分配temporal labels（保持N_ref=1080, N_foc=807）， 每次运行MH-DIF，建立C%的null distribution。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_permutations\": 1000,\n      \"null_distribution\": {\n        \"mean_c_pct\": 0.47,\n        \"sd_c_pct\": 0.13,\n        \"median_c_pct\": 0.45,\n        \"min_c_pct\": 0.1,\n        \"max_c_pct\": 1.02,\n        \"q95_c_pct\": 0.71,\n        \"q99_c_pct\": 0.84\n      },\n      \"observed_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"z_score\": 237.2,\n      \"p_value\": \"<0.001 (all 1000 permutations below observed)\",\n      \"empirical_p\": 0.0,\n      \"effect_size_ratio\": \"observed/null_mean = 66.6×\",\n      \"per_family_stratified\": {\n        \"status\": \"not executed pre-submission\",\n        \"rationale\": \"identified as potential rebuttal experiment; requires grouping models by family and permuting within strata\",\n        \"estimated_null_mean_if_stratified\": 0.52,\n        \"estimated_z_if_stratified\": \">200\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Permutation Null Distribution\",\n        \"content\": \"Null C% summary statistics + observed vs null comparison + z-score + empirical p\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Statistically unambiguous result。Median档reviewers接受statistical significance 但push for stronger controls（per-family stratification）。这是well-targeted reviewer request——the paper should preemptively address it using plan_022 de-duplication as evidence that family structure doesn't inflate C%, and offer stratified permutation as rebuttal experiment if needed。在median档下，plan_029成功但creates a follow-up obligation in rebuttal。\\n\\n\\nPermutation null在median档下成功确认31.3%远超chance（p<0.001, z>200）。Null distribution 的mean C%=0.47%与within-cohort random split的0.18%在同一量级，内部一致。这直接回应 \\\"is 31% above chance?\\\"质疑。但median档的nuance：1位reviewer接受permutation null但 要求additional controls——specifically per-family stratified permutation，因为如果 model families cluster by temporal cohort（2023多Llama-2，2024多Llama-3），简单 permutation可能underestimate null。这成为rebuttal experiment需求。Plan_022的 de-duplication分析（K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%）provides partial defense，但 reviewer要求的是stratified permutation而非cap-based de-duplication。这是median档 3-5个rebuttal issues之一。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"odds_ratio_regression_transparency\",\n    \"description\": \"补充pseudo R²=0.0007的透明度：odds ratio + 95% CI + McFadden/Nagelkerke R² + deviance ratio。增加item-level accuracy change predictor。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model1_domain_delta\": {\n        \"predictor\": \"subject-level accuracy change (2024-2023)\",\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0007,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0012,\n        \"aic\": 15545.2,\n        \"or_per_010_acc_change\": 1.55,\n        \"or_ci_per_010\": [\n          1.19,\n          2.03\n        ],\n        \"interpretation\": \"10pp domain improvement → 1.55× odds of DIF, but explains <0.2% variance\"\n      },\n      \"model2_domain_plus_items\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0423,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.072,\n        \"aic\": 14902.3,\n        \"domain_delta_or\": 0.73,\n        \"ctt_difficulty_or\": 0.78,\n        \"ctt_discrimination_or\": 1.51,\n        \"simpsons_paradox\": true,\n        \"interpretation\": \"Domain accuracy delta REVERSES direction after controlling for item properties — Simpson's paradox\"\n      },\n      \"model3_item_delta\": {\n        \"predictor\": \"item-level accuracy change (per-item 2024-2023 delta)\",\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0012,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0021,\n        \"aic\": 15536.9,\n        \"item_acc_change_or_per_010\": 1.08,\n        \"item_acc_change_ci\": [\n          1.51,\n          2.96\n        ]\n      },\n      \"model4_full\": {\n        \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.0434,\n        \"nagelkerke_r2\": 0.0737,\n        \"aic\": 14885.4,\n        \"item_delta_or\": 0.92,\n        \"difficulty_or\": 0.77,\n        \"discrimination_or\": 1.54,\n        \"lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2\": 655.53\n      },\n      \"simpsons_paradox_narrative\": \"\\\"Domain improvement predicts DIF marginally (OR=1.55), but this relationship REVERSES (OR=0.73) after controlling for item difficulty and discrimination. Items that are harder and more discriminating are more likely to show DIF, regardless of domain-level improvement. The 'models got better' story is a Simpson's paradox — improvement concentrates in domains with harder, more discriminating items.\\\"\\n\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Logistic Regression Decomposition\",\n        \"content\": \"4 models: domain Δ only → domain Δ + items → item Δ only → item Δ + items; OR, CI, R², AIC for each\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Key analytical contribution。在median档下Simpson's paradox被视为paper的most surprising finding之一，多数reviewers find it compelling。但endogeneity concern prevents full resolution of \\\"why 31%?\\\"——paper需honestly position这as \\\"DIF is predominantly item-specific, not domain-driven, but the causal direction between item properties and DIF remains ambiguous\\\"。这contributes to causal language hedging requirement。\\n\\nSimpson's paradox是median档下的strong defense line。Domain-level accuracy improvement 与DIF的marginal association（OR=1.55, R²<0.002）在控制item properties后reverses （OR=0.73），证明\\\"models got better\\\"不是DIF的driver——item difficulty和discrimination 才是。在median档下，这个result被2位reviewers接受为convincing decomposition evidence。 但1位reviewer质疑：\\\"item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — DIF items are harder BECAUSE they function differently across cohorts, not vice versa\\\"。 这是valid methodological point，paper需在limitations中acknowledge endogeneity concern。 Simpson's paradox被用在rebuttal中作为\\\"second line of defense\\\"（与plan_027 ability overlap d=-0.17并用）回应\\\"31% is just capability improvement\\\"质疑。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":660,"startLine":1,"totalLines":660}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DPgGMEf3wEeBNaKWz9GxR6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me also check the paper-writing-norms skill and the existing paper directory structure.\n\nLet me now write the complete LaTeX paper. I need to:\n\n1. Cover all experiments from experiment_data.json\n2. Follow the paper framing from paper_framing.md\n3. Target EMNLP 2026 (8-page limit, but this is a \"median\" tier dream paper - \"够审\" quality)\n4. Include Abstract, Introduction, Method, Experiments, Conclusion\n5. Each quantitative claim must be based on experiment_data.json\n\n\n6. Organize the paper with Abstract, Introduction (establishing the \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing), Related Work, and Method sections covering MH-DIF, the semi-synthetic framework, and cross-subject matching, then structure the experiments around temporal DIF on MMLU, cross-benchmark replication studies, and ground truth meta-critique analysis.\n\n7. Add sections for semi-synthetic validation, downstream impact assessment with degradation metrics and odds ratios, permutation null testing, and RL robustness checks, with supplementary material covering IFT, architecture variations, bifactor models, and Bayesian cumulative DIF approaches.\n\n8. Given the 8-page constraint, I need to be selective about what stays in the main body versus the appendix—most of the RL robustness work and supplementary analyses should move to the back, keeping the core temporal DIF claims and cross-benchmark validation as the centerpiece.\n\nNow I'm setting up the LaTeX document structure...\n\nGenerating markdown table... Logistic Regression Decomposition (from odds_ratio_regression_transparency)\n\nPlus appendix tables:\n- Table S1: RL Robustness (from rl_robustness_validation)\n- Table S2: Bayesian DIF Power (from cumulative_bayesian_dif)\n- Table S3: Graceful Degradation (from graceful_degradation_analysis)\n- Table S4: IFT vs MH-DIF (from item_focused_trees)\n\nI need to map all 12 experiments into the paper structure. The main results go in Section 4.1 with real_data_dif_mmlu, while cross_benchmark_gsm8k and semi_synthetic_contamination_validation become Section 4.3, and multi_benchmark_temporal_dif covers Section 4.2. The robustness validation and graceful degradation analysis support the limitations and claims in Sections 5 and 4.4 respectively. A few experiments like constat_perturbation_eval and dvd_generation_variance_eval weren't executed so I'll mention them in related work, while ensemble_fusion and item_generation_calibration get deferred to future work, and bifactor_irt_equating_pilot gets a brief note in the limitations. Writing the LaTeX paper...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14365,"cache_read_input_tokens":24322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14365},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68384416-f199-481e-b490-5f37e9ab5fc0","uuid":"e89fd354-e430-4bf0-b018-aace9559d7a6"}
